Privacy Policy
Effective Date: September 8, 2026
This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, store, protect, and disclose information when you access or use the VishuShethra mobile application ("App") and our website, https://vishushethra.com/ ("Website").
By using our App or Website, you agree to the practices described in this Privacy Policy.
1. Information We May Collect
Depending on how you use our App or Website, we may collect information that you voluntarily provide to us, including:
•	Name
•	Mobile number
•	Email address
•	Business or company information
•	Address or location information, where required for providing a requested service
•	Product or service enquiry details
•	Information submitted through contact or enquiry forms
•	Any other information that you voluntarily provide while communicating with us
We may also automatically receive certain technical information when you use our App or Website, such as:
•	Device type
•	Operating system
•	Browser or application information
•	IP address
•	General usage information
•	Application or website interaction information
•	Technical information necessary for security, troubleshooting, and improving our services
We only seek to collect information that is reasonably necessary for providing and improving our services.


2. How We Use Your Information
The information we collect may be used for purposes including:
•	Responding to your enquiries and requests
•	Providing information about our products and services
•	Communicating with customers and prospective customers
•	Processing and managing business enquiries
•	Improving our App, Website, products, and services
•	Providing customer support
•	Maintaining security and preventing misuse
•	Troubleshooting technical issues
•	Maintaining business and service records
•	Complying with applicable legal and regulatory requirements
We will not use your personal information for purposes that are incompatible with the purpose for which it was collected, except where permitted or required by applicable law.
3. Location Information
Certain features of the App or Website may request access to location information.
Location access, where requested, may be used to provide location-related functionality or improve the user experience.
You may control location permissions through your device settings. If you deny location permission, certain location-dependent features may not function properly.
We do not use location information for purposes unrelated to the functionality for which it is requested.
4. Cookies and Similar Technologies
Our Website or services may use cookies or similar technologies to improve functionality, understand usage, maintain sessions, and enhance the user experience.
Cookies may collect technical or usage-related information. You can control or disable cookies through your browser settings. However, disabling certain cookies may affect the functionality of some features.
5. Sharing of Information
We do not sell, rent, or trade your personal information to third parties for their independent marketing purposes.
We may share information when reasonably necessary with:
•	Service providers who assist us in operating our Website or App
•	Technical, hosting, analytics, or infrastructure service providers
•	Professional advisors where necessary
•	Government authorities or law-enforcement agencies when required by applicable law
•	Other parties where disclosure is necessary to protect our legal rights, safety, property, or users
Any third-party service providers receiving information from us are expected to handle such information appropriately and only for the purposes for which it is provided.
6. Third-Party Links and Services
Our App or Website may contain links to third-party websites, services, social media platforms, or other external resources.
If you access a third-party service through our App or Website, that service may have its own privacy policy and terms of use.
We are not responsible for the privacy practices, content, security, or policies of third-party websites or services. We encourage users to review the applicable privacy policies before providing personal information to third parties.
7. Data Security
We take reasonable technical and organizational measures to protect personal information against unauthorized access, misuse, alteration, disclosure, loss, or destruction.
However, no electronic transmission or storage system can be guaranteed to be completely secure. Therefore, while we take reasonable steps to protect information, we cannot guarantee absolute security.
8. Data Retention
We retain personal information only for as long as reasonably necessary to:
•	Provide our services
•	Respond to enquiries
•	Maintain appropriate business records
•	Fulfil legal, regulatory, accounting, or reporting requirements
•	Resolve disputes and enforce applicable agreements
When information is no longer required for these purposes, it may be deleted, anonymized, or securely disposed of, subject to applicable legal requirements.
9. Children's Privacy
Our App and Website are intended for general audiences and are not specifically directed toward children.
We do not knowingly collect personal information from children where such collection is prohibited by applicable law.
If a parent or legal guardian believes that a child has provided personal information to us without appropriate authorization, they may contact us so that we can review and take appropriate action.
10. Your Privacy Rights
Subject to applicable law, you may have the right to:
•	Request access to personal information held about you
•	Request correction of inaccurate information
•	Request deletion of information where legally applicable
•	Withdraw consent where processing is based on consent
•	Raise questions, grievances, or concerns regarding our handling of personal information
To exercise any applicable privacy rights, please contact us using the details provided below.
11. Withdrawal of Consent
Where we process personal information based on your consent, you may withdraw your consent by contacting us.
Please note that withdrawing consent may affect our ability to provide certain features, products, or services where the information is necessary for providing them.
Withdrawal of consent will not affect processing that has already been carried out lawfully before the withdrawal.
12. Governing Law and Jurisdiction
This Privacy Policy and any disputes or claims arising out of or in connection with it shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of India. You agree that the courts located in Chennai, Tamil Nadu, shall have exclusive jurisdiction over any legal matters arising from the use of our App or Website.
13. Changes to This Privacy Policy
We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect changes in our services, technology, legal requirements, or business practices.
Any updated Privacy Policy will be published on this page with a revised "Effective Date."
We encourage users to review this page periodically for the latest information regarding our privacy practices.
14. Contact Us
If you have any questions, concerns, requests, or complaints regarding this Privacy Policy or the handling of your personal information (including grievances under applicable Indian data protection regulations), please contact VishuShethra Industries.
